---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { MODE, base } from '../../lib/data';
---
<Layout title="3D viewer" description="Interactive decimated point clouds, ICP before and after, and trajectories.">
  <section class="wrap section">
    <p class="caption">D · Interactive 3D</p>
    <h2>Point clouds and trajectories</h2>
    <p class="muted">Decimated excerpts generated by the pipeline (at most a few thousand points per layer, uint16-quantised). Drag to rotate, scroll to zoom, right-drag to pan.</p>
    <div id="viewer" data-base={base} data-mode={MODE} class="grid" style="grid-template-columns:minmax(0,2fr) minmax(260px,1fr);align-items:start">
      <div class="card" style="padding:0;overflow:hidden"><canvas id="gl" style="width:100%;height:520px;display:block" aria-label="3D point cloud view" role="img"></canvas></div>
      <div class="card">
        <label class="caption" for="run">Run</label><br /><select id="run" style="width:100%"></select>
        <div class="grid cols-2" style="margin-top:12px;gap:8px">
          <div><label class="caption" for="view">View</label><br /><select id="view" style="width:100%"><option value="clouds">Point clouds</option><option value="trajectory">Trajectories</option></select></div>
          <div><label class="caption" for="pair">Pair</label><br /><select id="pair" style="width:100%"><option value="typical">Typical</option><option value="worst">Slowest</option></select></div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top:12px"><label class="caption" for="size">Point size</label><br /><input id="size" type="range" min="1" max="6" step="0.5" value="2" style="width:100%" /></p>
        <p><label><input id="axes" type="checkbox" checked /> Coordinate frame (1 m axes)</label></p>
        <button id="flip" class="outline" type="button">Before / after registration</button>
        <p class="caption" style="margin-top:16px">Layers</p>
        <div id="layers"></div>
        <p class="caption" style="margin-top:16px">Colours</p>
        <p style="margin:0"><span style="color:var(--viz-source)">■</span> source · <span style="color:var(--viz-target)">■</span> target · <span style="color:var(--viz-estimate)">■</span> estimate · <span style="color:var(--viz-truth)">■</span> ground truth · greys: processing stages</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="provenance" class="card alt" style="margin-top:16px"></div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top:16px">
      <h3>What to observe</h3>
      <ul style="padding-left:18px;margin:0">
        <li><b>Stages</b>: raw → range-filtered → voxel-filtered clouds show how many points each step removes and that the structure that matters for matching survives.</li>
        <li><b>Before / after</b>: the source (blue) is moved onto the target (orange). Alignment of walls and ground planes after registration is the evidence that this pair registered; the numbers for the pair are in the provenance panel.</li>
        <li><b>Trajectories</b>: estimate (violet) against ground truth (black) after a rigid alignment. They can agree closely over a short window and still drift over distance.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3 style="margin-top:12px">What can be concluded</h3>
      <p>Only that the shown pairs and window behaved as described. Excerpts are chosen by rule (median and slowest pair), not to flatter. They do not show real-time capability, other scenes or other hardware.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script>import '../../scripts/viewer.ts';</script>
</Layout>